 "voice": {
  "text": "Its tip was once a luxury. In 1884, the tallest structure on Earth was capped with a 100-ounce pyramid of a rare metal. So which metal? Aluminium. It was so hard to make that it was worth about as much as silver. Then in 1886, two young chemists, one in America and one in France, found an electric method that made it cheap. Today it is in cans and foil, and the 8.9-inch pyramid still helps carry lightning to the ground. Turns out, the tallest tower on Earth wore a precious metal tip, and within years that metal became cheap.",
