 "caption": "Which metal do you think topped the Washington Monument in 1884? 🗼\n\nWhen the tower was finished it was the tallest structure on Earth, and its tip was a 100-ounce pyramid of aluminium, then a metal so hard to make that it was about as precious as silver. Two years later, in 1886, Charles Martin Hall in the USA and Paul Héroult in France found an electric method that made aluminium cheap. The 8.9-inch pyramid is still up there, and it helps carry lightning to the ground.\n\nSend this to the friend who thinks aluminium was always cheap.\n\nImages: IMAGES_LINE",
